    "Next to the middle lamella, each cell has its primary cell wall."
   ],
   [
    13.815,
    "It is relatively thin and flexible, so a growing cell can still stretch."
   ],
   [
    18.789,
    "Some cells also add a secondary cell wall."
   ],
   [
    21.68,
    "It goes between the plasma membrane and the primary wall, and it is thick and strong."
   ],
   [
    27.122,
    "That is why wood is hard."
   ],
   [
    28.646,
    "A tree trunk is mostly secondary walls."
   ],
   [
    31.589,
    "So from the middle outward, it goes middle lamella, primary wall, secondary wall, and then the plasma membrane."
   ]
  ]
 },
